  "body": "Found in #9 round 2. A bar with a partial-lap flat (D-flat) longer than the axis-fit sphere guard reaches the wrap, which then fails with \"the mesh is open\" (4, 8 or 16 loose chord ends across three fixture variants). This blocks an end-to-end test of #9's seam law (a level whose centre component reaches a cover end short of a full lap is refused for Adaptive by name and cut by Offset rings); the seam rule is only unit-tested (machining3d::hsm::tests::the_seam_cuts_an_area_at_a_cover_end_short_of_a_lap).\n\nDone means: a D-flat bar wraps (or is refused by name before the wrap with the reason), and an integration test in crates/motion/tests/rotary_adaptive.rs proves the seam refusal names the level and Offset rings cut it.",
